{"id":62,"name":"poliwrath","speciesId":62,"dex":62,"form":"normal","generation":1,"types":["water","fighting"],"stats":{"hp":90,"attack":95,"defense":95,"special-attack":70,"special-defense":90,"speed":70},"abilities":[{"name":"water-absorb","hidden":false},{"name":"damp","hidden":false},{"name":"swift-swim","hidden":true}],"height":13,"weight":540,"baseExp":230,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/62.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/62.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/62.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/62.ogg","genus":"Tadpole Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"red","text":"An adept swimmer at both the front crawl and breast stroke. Easily overtakes the best human swimmers."},{"version":"yellow","text":"Swims powerfully using all the muscles in its body. It can even overtake champion swimmers."},{"version":"gold","text":"This strong and skilled swimmer is even capable of crossing the Pacific Ocean just by kicking."},{"version":"silver","text":"Although an ener­ getic, skilled swimmer that uses all of its mus­ cles, it lives on dry land."},{"version":"crystal","text":"It can use its well-developed arms and legs to run on the surface of the water for a split second."},{"version":"ruby","text":"POLIWRATH’s highly developed, brawny muscles never grow fatigued, however much it exercises. It is so tirelessly strong, this POKéMON can swim back and forth across the Pacific Ocean without effort."},{"version":"emerald","text":"Its highly developed muscles never grow fatigued, however much it exercises. This POKéMON can swim back and forth across the Pacific Ocean without effort."},{"version":"firered","text":"An adept swimmer, it knows the front crawl, butterfly, and more. It is faster than the best human swimmers."},{"version":"leafgreen","text":"A swimmer adept at both the front crawl and breaststroke. Easily overtakes the best human swimmers."},{"version":"diamond","text":"With its extremely tough muscles, it can keep swimming in the Pacific Ocean without resting."},{"version":"soulsilver","text":"Although an energetic, skilled swimmer that uses all of its muscles, it lives on dry land."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Poliwrath’s highly developed, brawny muscles never grow fatigued, however much it exercises. It is so tirelessly strong, this Pokémon can swim back and forth across the ocean without effort."},{"version":"sun","text":"Poliwrath in the Alola region are strong swimmers that use the breaststroke. Many children learn to swim by imitating Poliwrath."},{"version":"moon","text":"Its percentage of body fat is nearly zero. Its body is entirely muscle, which makes it heavy and forces its swimming prowess to develop."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"It’s quite a gifted swimmer, even among Water-type Pokémon, but it normally spends its time on land."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"The muscles it has developed through swimming are thick and powerful. When it lands a square punch, it can turn huge boulders to dust."},{"version":"lets-go-pikachu","text":"Swims powerfully using all the muscles in its body. It can even overtake world-class swimmers."},{"version":"sword","text":"Its body is solid muscle. When swimming through cold seas, Poliwrath uses its impressive arms to smash through drift ice and plow forward."},{"version":"shield","text":"Poliwrath is skilled at both swimming and martial arts. It uses its well-trained arms to dish out powerful punches."}],"genderRate":4,"captureRate":45,"eggGroups":["water1"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"poliwag","speciesId":60,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Nível 25"],"species":"poliwhirl","speciesId":61,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Usar Water Stone"],"species":"poliwrath","speciesId":62,"evolvesTo